        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2015. Published by Elsevier Ltd.",
        "AbstractText": "Dendritic cells (DCs) regulate the generation of effector adaptive immunity and enforce peripheral tolerance. In the October 2015 issue of Immunity, Zlotnikov-Klionsky et al. present exciting data describing a population of perforin-expressing CD11c(+)DCs that limit obesity as well as metabolic and autoimmune inflammation in mice."
